      "headline": "Astonishing mod runs DLSS 5 on a second GPU to boost neural-rendered FPS up to 127% — game renders on one card, neural post-processing runs on the other, much like dedicated PhysX GPUs",
      "confirmed_facts": [
        {
          "fact_id": "f1",
          "text": "Astonishing mod runs DLSS 5 on a second GPU to boost neural-rendered FPS up to 127% — game renders on one card, neural post-processing runs on the other, much like dedicated PhysX GPUs Harkening back to the days of PhysX.",
          "source_id": "source:primary",
          "captured_at": "2026-09-08T08:04:58.636422+08:00",
          "content_sha256": "d35c4e53ecd4e9bcd6124861ae0930bd21e233314e6061ee84ff8db924fdbae5",
          "excerpt": "Astonishing mod runs DLSS 5 on a second GPU to boost neural-rendered FPS up to 127% — game renders on one card, neural post-processing runs on the other, much like dedicated PhysX GPUs Harkening back to the days of PhysX.",
          "sentence_hash": "4bef8f094dd16549bf1ab3f5ebac78402e185ae567452d49bf160eb8934922e7",
          "anchors": [
            "127%",
            "neural"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact_id": "f2",
          "text": "Nvidia's DLSS 5 Neural Rendering technology has taken the PC gaming world by storm since its recent leak and then official rollout in recent days.",
          "source_id": "source:primary",
          "captured_at": "2026-09-08T08:04:58.636457+08:00",
          "content_sha256": "d35c4e53ecd4e9bcd6124861ae0930bd21e233314e6061ee84ff8db924fdbae5",
          "excerpt": "Nvidia's DLSS 5 Neural Rendering technology has taken the PC gaming world by storm since its recent leak and then official rollout in recent days.",
          "sentence_hash": "7bc6e1f9e71cc1a505d55bad2a80fc6c97c633d9d8bb71e88fe63e8e974b63e5",
          "anchors": [
            "its"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact_id": "f3",
          "text": "In what might be one of the most impressive technical applications and mods of the feature yet, one developer has showcased DLSS 5 running on a second GPU to share the processing load, rendering the game on the first GPU before applying Neural rendering at the end of the frame, t",
          "source_id": "source:primary",
          "captured_at": "2026-09-08T08:04:58.636493+08:00",
          "content_sha256": "d35c4e53ecd4e9bcd6124861ae0930bd21e233314e6061ee84ff8db924fdbae5",
          "excerpt": "In what might be one of the most impressive technical applications and mods of the feature yet, one developer has showcased DLSS 5 running on a second GPU to share the processing load, rendering the game on the first GPU before applying Neural rendering at the end of the frame, t",
          "sentence_hash": "ec661d57240983cade44c23dbcb58dcceb21025769c135cad62447f1556466bd",
          "anchors": [
            "neural"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact_id": "f4",
          "text": "The add-on creates its own D3D12 device on your second GPU, sends each finished frame across to it, runs DLSS-NR there, and displays the result on that card's own monitor — so nothing has to come back.",
          "source_id": "source:primary",
          "captured_at": "2026-09-08T08:04:58.636559+08:00",
          "content_sha256": "d35c4e53ecd4e9bcd6124861ae0930bd21e233314e6061ee84ff8db924fdbae5",
          "excerpt": "The add-on creates its own D3D12 device on your second GPU, sends each finished frame across to it, runs DLSS-NR there, and displays the result on that card's own monitor — so nothing has to come back.",
          "sentence_hash": "fa8311827f1543e5cf20801444927d7fb6c000ddba1d5fc3e75db9a4d9c9834c",
          "anchors": [
            "its",
            "the re"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact_id": "f5",
          "text": "The render GPU does no neural work at all and runs cooler for the same reason.\" In the TBOD demo at 1080p, they shared the following performance numbers: Guibout clarified that DLSS super-resolution is running in every column of the test, with the rows showing each mode tested.",
          "source_id": "source:primary",
          "captured_at": "2026-09-08T08:04:58.636591+08:00",
          "content_sha256": "d35c4e53ecd4e9bcd6124861ae0930bd21e233314e6061ee84ff8db924fdbae5",
          "excerpt": "The render GPU does no neural work at all and runs cooler for the same reason.\" In the TBOD demo at 1080p, they shared the following performance numbers: Guibout clarified that DLSS super-resolution is running in every column of the test, with the rows showing each mode tested.",
          "sentence_hash": "e428349566bc4fbdb787527802e35b930749f7cc7cee7821e527ca73e6c839f6",
          "anchors": [
            "neural"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact_id": "f6",
          "text": "The game rendered at the same internal resolution in all three columns, with the first column giving figures with DLSS 5's neural rendering switched off, representing the ceiling for performance.",
          "source_id": "source:primary",
          "captured_at": "2026-09-08T08:04:58.636614+08:00",
          "content_sha256": "d35c4e53ecd4e9bcd6124861ae0930bd21e233314e6061ee84ff8db924fdbae5",
          "excerpt": "The game rendered at the same internal resolution in all three columns, with the first column giving figures with DLSS 5's neural rendering switched off, representing the ceiling for performance.",
          "sentence_hash": "0cb762e0f6f3508c45e0a27a9d848c6e2ddc0a227845e1a2506e67414f762b2d",
